From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] hwservicemanager: a caller without a security context is the normal case

apklayer's libhwbinder carries no TXN_SECURITY_CTX (patches/aosp/system/libhwbinder 0001), so getCallingSid() is always null; the tree's
CHECK_EQ on the serving stack pointer then aborted hwservicemanager at the first transaction ("Pid N missing service context"). The call falls
through to AccessControl::getCallingContext(pid), which apklayer's allow-all AccessControl answers.
Against system/hwservicemanager 60271965cf6b (REVISION), after 0001. Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/ServiceManager.cpp b/ServiceManager.cpp
--- a/ServiceManager.cpp
+++ b/ServiceManager.cpp
@@ -47,9 +47,6 @@ AccessControl::CallingContext getBinderCallingContext() {
             android_errorWriteLog(0x534e4554, "121035042");
         }

-        CHECK_EQ(nullptr, self->getServingStackPointer())
-                << "Pid " << pid << " missing service context.";
-
         return AccessControl::getCallingContext(pid);
     } else {
         return { true, sid, pid };
